WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.060 --> 00:00:04.020
Reed Richard's descendant? Inspired by Doctor&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:04.020 --> 00:00:07.884
Doom? Here's the truth about&nbsp;
Ant-Man 3's Kang: The Conquerer!

00:00:08.400 --> 00:00:12.840
Although "Ant-Man &amp; the Wasp: Quantumania"&nbsp;
will be the official debut of the menace&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:12.840 --> 00:00:17.160
known as Kang the Conqueror, it's not&nbsp;
Jonathan Majors' first rodeo in the MCU.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:17.160 --> 00:00:22.500
The actor played the role of He Who Remains in&nbsp;
the first season finale of "Loki," revealed to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:22.500 --> 00:00:27.060
be the mastermind behind the Time-Keepers&nbsp;
and the Time Variance Authority. However,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:27.060 --> 00:00:30.900
the character's ties to Kang the&nbsp;
Conqueror were worn on his sleeve.

00:00:31.500 --> 00:00:35.580
"You're a flea on the back of a&nbsp;
dragon in for one hell of a ride."

00:00:36.180 --> 00:00:40.560
After Loki and Sylvie confront He Who&nbsp;
Remains at the Citadel at the End of Time,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:40.560 --> 00:00:45.840
Majors' character reveals his backstory, which&nbsp;
just so happens to be the same as Kang's from&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:45.840 --> 00:00:50.340
the comics. He Who Remains was originally&nbsp;
a scientist from the 31st century who,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:50.340 --> 00:00:54.180
after discovering the existence of the&nbsp;
multiverse, used it to make contact with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:54.180 --> 00:00:59.100
his variants across space and time. Sooner&nbsp;
or later, some of those variants waged war&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:59.100 --> 00:01:03.900
in pursuit of conquering the multiverse,&nbsp;
and once He Who Remains came out on top,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:03.900 --> 00:01:09.360
he isolated the Sacred Timeline and created&nbsp;
the TVA to prune any unwanted branches.

00:01:09.360 --> 00:01:13.920
Majors' performance in the "Loki"&nbsp;
finale was well-received, especially&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:13.920 --> 00:01:19.500
by MCU fans who had correctly theorized Kang's&nbsp;
involvement in the earlier episodes. However,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:19.500 --> 00:01:22.860
the character's presence was a clear&nbsp;
warning sign of what's to come,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:22.860 --> 00:01:27.188
with the series' head writer Michael Waldron&nbsp;
saying in an interview with Marvel.com,

00:01:33.600 --> 00:01:37.800
He Who Remains, while being&nbsp;
an interpretation of Kang the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:37.800 --> 00:01:42.120
Conqueror himself, also has his own ties&nbsp;
to Marvel's comic book origins. However,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:42.120 --> 00:01:46.800
his main inspiration is not the character of&nbsp;
the same name, who created both the Time-Keepers&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:46.800 --> 00:01:51.840
and TVA in the comics and first debuted in&nbsp;
the 1970s. No, the MCU iteration of He Who&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:51.840 --> 00:01:57.120
Remains actually has much more in common&nbsp;
with a specific variant of Kang: Immortus.

00:01:57.120 --> 00:02:01.080
In the comics, Immortus was a version&nbsp;
of Kang who grew tired of conquering&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:01.080 --> 00:02:05.520
and retreated to a dimension outside&nbsp;
of space and time known as Limbo,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:05.520 --> 00:02:09.660
which bears a lot of similarity&nbsp;
to "The Void" in "Loki." There,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:09.660 --> 00:02:14.280
Immortus got in contact with the Time-Keepers,&nbsp;
who offered him the job of influencing events&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:14.280 --> 00:02:19.080
in the Sacred Timeline to prevent mankind&nbsp;
from straying off their planned destinies.

00:02:19.080 --> 00:02:24.240
The MCU version of He Who Remains is a composite&nbsp;
of both the original He Who Remains from the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:24.240 --> 00:02:28.560
comics and Immortus. This is reflected in the&nbsp;
character's clothing in the "Loki" finale,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:28.560 --> 00:02:33.120
which combines the familiar purple-and-green&nbsp;
colors of Immortus with the comfort of He&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:33.120 --> 00:02:37.860
Who Remains' robes. In "The Making of&nbsp;
Loki" on Disney+, Majors reveals He&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:37.860 --> 00:02:42.660
Who Remains' outfit also drew inspiration&nbsp;
from Genghis Khan and the Victorian era.

00:02:43.140 --> 00:02:48.420
Although he's mainly known for his antagonistic&nbsp;
role as Kang the Conqueror, the character's long&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:48.420 --> 00:02:54.660
and storied past ties him to one of Marvel's most&nbsp;
popular teams. Before he traveled the multiverse,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:54.660 --> 00:03:00.180
conquering and ruling, Kang was an Earthly&nbsp;
scientist named Nathaniel Richards. Despite&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:00.180 --> 00:03:05.040
living in the 31st century, Kang's heritage&nbsp;
traces all the way back to none other than&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:05.040 --> 00:03:09.720
Reed Richards, the smartest man alive&nbsp;
and the leader of the Fantastic Four.

00:03:09.720 --> 00:03:14.820
Even though the cast of Matt Shakman's upcoming&nbsp;
MCU Fantastic Four film has yet to be announced,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:14.820 --> 00:03:19.980
Reed Richards, like Kang, also made his&nbsp;
MCU debut in Phase 4. He was portrayed by&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:19.980 --> 00:03:23.520
John Krasinski in a brief appearance&nbsp;
in "Doctor Strange in the Multiverse&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:23.520 --> 00:03:27.360
of Madness." Given the Fantastic&nbsp;
Four's impending arrival in the MCU,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:27.360 --> 00:03:31.500
as well as their importance in the comic&nbsp;
book events of "Secret Wars," there's no&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:31.500 --> 00:03:36.480
doubt that Kang and the Fantastic Four will&nbsp;
inevitably cross paths on the big screen.

00:03:36.480 --> 00:03:41.280
However, Kang the Conqueror's ties to Reed&nbsp;
Richards may be even more complex than that.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:41.280 --> 00:03:46.080
Comic book fans will know that Reed Richards'&nbsp;
father also happened to be named Nathaniel.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:46.080 --> 00:03:51.480
Some theorists have speculated that Reed&nbsp;
Richards' father was yet another variant of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:51.480 --> 00:03:57.540
Kang the Conqueror, who traveled back in time and&nbsp;
created his own legacy. Perhaps this will prove&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:57.540 --> 00:04:03.637
to be an important aspect of Kang's character&nbsp;
in the 2026 film "Avengers: The Kang Dynasty."

00:04:03.660 --> 00:04:09.600
Kang the Conqueror's Fantastic Four ties don't&nbsp;
stop with his lineage. The character also draws&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:09.600 --> 00:04:15.660
plenty of inspiration from one of the biggest&nbsp;
and most popular Fantastic Four antagonists:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:15.660 --> 00:04:20.460
Doctor Doom. Fan anticipation and&nbsp;
speculation regarding the official&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:20.460 --> 00:04:25.500
MCU introduction of Doctor Doom remains some&nbsp;
of the highest the film franchise has seen&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:25.500 --> 00:04:29.340
to date. The character is closely tied to&nbsp;
the events of "Secret Wars" in the comics,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:29.340 --> 00:04:32.700
and his full potential has yet&nbsp;
to be realized on the big screen.

00:04:32.700 --> 00:04:37.200
Of course, the introduction of Kang and&nbsp;
the promise of the Fantastic Four means&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:37.200 --> 00:04:42.480
Victor von Doom is on a collision course&nbsp;
with the MCU. Having been defeated by the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:42.480 --> 00:04:46.440
Fantastic Four in the comics, one variant&nbsp;
of Kang ends up encountering Doctor Doom&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:46.440 --> 00:04:50.520
in the 20th century. Inspired by the&nbsp;
Latverian conqueror, this version of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:50.520 --> 00:04:55.800
Kang dubs himself the Scarlet Centurion and&nbsp;
forces the Avengers to face their alternate&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:55.800 --> 00:05:00.720
selves in a multiversal war. He even takes&nbsp;
inspiration from Doom's outfit for his own.

00:05:00.720 --> 00:05:07.440
For Kang's MCU future, it's possible he'll be&nbsp;
inspired by Doom in any number of ways. Donning a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:07.440 --> 00:05:12.360
similar outfit as Doom is certainly a possibility,&nbsp;
as is pitting the Avengers against each other as&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:12.360 --> 00:05:17.340
the main plot of "Avengers: Secret Wars." From&nbsp;
the look of Jonathan Majors' Kang in the first&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:17.340 --> 00:05:23.640
trailer for "Ant-Man &amp; the Wasp: Quantumania," it&nbsp;
seems his outfit already has Doctor Doom vibes.

00:05:24.240 --> 00:05:28.140
There are many other Kang the Conqueror&nbsp;
variants whose comic book iterations may&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:28.140 --> 00:05:31.860
influence the look of Jonathan Majors'&nbsp;
portrayal in "Ant-Man &amp; the Wasp:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:31.860 --> 00:05:36.660
Quantumania," as well as future appearances in&nbsp;
the MCU. One of the earlier versions of Kang&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:36.660 --> 00:05:41.340
to debut in the comics appears after Nathaniel&nbsp;
Richards time-travels to Ancient Egypt. There,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:41.340 --> 00:05:46.440
he becomes a ruler and worshiped figure amongst&nbsp;
the Egyptians under the moniker "Rama-Tut."

00:05:46.440 --> 00:05:51.120
Of course, Kang the Conqueror's affiliation with&nbsp;
Ancient Egypt in the comics perfectly lends the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:51.120 --> 00:05:55.200
Marvel Cinematic Universe the opportunity to&nbsp;
have the character come to blows with Moon&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:55.200 --> 00:06:00.300
Knight and Khonshu. This comic book premise&nbsp;
is an early storyline for the Fantastic Four,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:00.300 --> 00:06:04.320
who find themselves taken prisoner by&nbsp;
Rama-Tut in the past. It's possible that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:04.320 --> 00:06:08.760
this storyline could serve as the basis&nbsp;
for the upcoming Fantastic Four movie,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:08.760 --> 00:06:14.040
which would mean that Jonathan Majors' Kang could&nbsp;
take on the appearance of an Egyptian pharaoh.

00:06:14.040 --> 00:06:18.360
Nevertheless, it's also possible that the&nbsp;
upcoming Fantastic Four film will revolve&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:18.360 --> 00:06:22.560
around the original team's encounters with the&nbsp;
Skrulls, who have also already made their MCU&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:22.560 --> 00:06:27.300
debut. Perhaps Kang the Conqueror's relationship&nbsp;
with ancient Egypt will be explored through his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:27.300 --> 00:06:32.520
costume design in future films such as "The Kang&nbsp;
Dynasty," or even in the second season of "Loki."

00:06:32.940 --> 00:06:37.380
When Majors' appearance in the third "Ant-Man"&nbsp;
movie as Marvel supervillain Kang the Conqueror&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:37.380 --> 00:06:42.360
was first announced, many fans were rightfully&nbsp;
surprised. Given the light-hearted nature of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:42.360 --> 00:06:47.940
Paul Rudd's MCU franchise, it seemed like an&nbsp;
odd couple to pair his smarmy thief with one&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:47.940 --> 00:06:53.280
of the cruelest and most sinister characters&nbsp;
that Marvel has to offer. Nevertheless, the two&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:53.280 --> 00:06:58.945
are set to square off in the Marvel Cinematic&nbsp;
Universe's highly-anticipated start to 2023.

00:06:58.945 --> 00:07:04.885
"So, what's it gonna be, Ant-Man?"

00:07:05.220 --> 00:07:09.600
The first trailers for "Ant-Man &amp; the Wasp:&nbsp;
Quantumania" have given insight into what&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:09.600 --> 00:07:14.040
beef there will be between Kang the Conqueror&nbsp;
and Scott Lang. After accidentally ending up&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:14.040 --> 00:07:17.940
in the Quantum Realm, it appears that Kang&nbsp;
is hiring Scott to perform a heist for him,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:17.940 --> 00:07:21.420
which is certainly in Scott's skill&nbsp;
set, even in another dimension.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:21.420 --> 00:07:25.860
Fans have speculated that Kang wants&nbsp;
Scott to steal back his Time Chair,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:25.860 --> 00:07:30.660
which is what Kang uses to time-travel. Other&nbsp;
fan speculation theorizes that the current&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:30.660 --> 00:07:35.580
owner of Kang's Time Chair is none other than&nbsp;
MODOK, who's also set to appear in the film.

00:07:35.580 --> 00:07:40.620
Some fans believe the Time Chair can be&nbsp;
spotted in one of the first trailers to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:40.620 --> 00:07:45.540
"Ant-Man 3," depicting Kang standing in front&nbsp;
of it wearing a very comic-accurate costume.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:45.540 --> 00:07:49.260
Though it's unclear why Kang wants&nbsp;
his precious time-travel device back,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:49.260 --> 00:07:54.240
one can assume he plans to use it for the&nbsp;
purpose of doing what he does best: conquering.

00:07:54.720 --> 00:07:59.640
The presence of another significant Marvel&nbsp;
baddie, MODOK, may also allude to a much&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:59.640 --> 00:08:03.540
different path for Kang the Conqueror than&nbsp;
fans are anticipating. In Marvel Comics,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:03.540 --> 00:08:08.880
there's precedent set for Kang to have a change of&nbsp;
heart. One teenage variant of Nathaniel Richards&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:08.880 --> 00:08:13.500
encounters his future self a bit early, when&nbsp;
Kang time-travels to protect his younger self&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:13.500 --> 00:08:18.900
from a life-altering injury. Taking the younger&nbsp;
Nathaniel Richards under his wing, Kang attempts&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:18.900 --> 00:08:24.600
to show himself the legendary ruler he'd become,&nbsp;
only for this lecture to frighten him instead.

00:08:24.600 --> 00:08:30.420
In an attempt to reverse his destiny, this&nbsp;
Nathaniel Richards assembles a Young Avengers&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:30.420 --> 00:08:35.760
team, with himself as their leader, wearing&nbsp;
a Stark-esque suit and donning the name "Iron&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:35.760 --> 00:08:40.740
Lad." His teammates include several characters who&nbsp;
have already made their Marvel Cinematic Universe&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:40.740 --> 00:08:46.560
debuts, including Kate Bishop, Elijah Bradley,&nbsp;
and Wanda's twin sons. One of Richards' other&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:46.560 --> 00:08:51.960
assembled teammates is Cassie Lang, with whom he&nbsp;
crosses paths during the events of "Quantumania."

00:08:51.960 --> 00:08:56.340
Despite reports of Majors' role as the&nbsp;
next Thanos-level threat in the MCU,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:56.340 --> 00:09:00.540
the plot of "Ant-Man 3" could take a&nbsp;
sharp turn with Kang having a moment of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:00.540 --> 00:09:03.744
redemption. With the Young Avengers&nbsp;
potentially being on the horizon,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:03.744 --> 00:09:09.204
the debut of Jonathan Majors, or another actor,&nbsp;
as Iron Lad could come much sooner than later.

00:09:09.840 --> 00:09:13.620
Another "Quantumania" theory concerns&nbsp;
a certain casting announcement from&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:13.620 --> 00:09:17.940
2022. To the surprise of many fans,&nbsp;
"The Good Place" star William Jackson&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:17.940 --> 00:09:21.960
Harper was confirmed to be appearing&nbsp;
in Peyton Reed's third "Ant-Man" film.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:21.960 --> 00:09:26.220
What's even more interesting is that the&nbsp;
actor's role is apparently top secret.

00:09:26.220 --> 00:09:31.320
Though it's more than likely Harper will join&nbsp;
Bill Murray as some sort of citizen living in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:31.320 --> 00:09:37.020
the Quantum Place, some fans speculate something&nbsp;
much more significant for the actor. Notably,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:37.020 --> 00:09:40.860
he's been a frontrunner of many&nbsp;
fan-castings for the Fantastic Four,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:40.860 --> 00:09:45.780
particularly in the role of Reed Richards,&nbsp;
per The AV Club. Harper's role as Chidi on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:45.780 --> 00:09:51.060
"The Good Place" certainly shows he's qualified to&nbsp;
capture the awkwardness and physique of Marvel's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:51.060 --> 00:09:55.920
smartest man alive. This is especially&nbsp;
true after rumors that John Krasinski's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:55.920 --> 00:10:00.240
cameo as Richards in "Doctor Strange in the&nbsp;
Multiverse of Madness" was a one-off appearance.

00:10:00.240 --> 00:10:05.400
However, Harper's potential casting as Reed&nbsp;
Richards could also prove very relevant to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:05.400 --> 00:10:09.660
the appearance of Kang the Conqueror. Given&nbsp;
the comic book origins of Kang as a descendant&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:09.660 --> 00:10:15.180
of Reed Richards, it would make some sense for&nbsp;
William Jackson Harper to be cast as the ancestor&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:15.180 --> 00:10:19.320
to Jonathan Majors. The only thing throwing&nbsp;
this theory off is other rumors surrounding&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:19.320 --> 00:10:24.809
Fantastic Four casting options, including&nbsp;
Penn Badgley and Adam Driver, via The Direct.

00:10:25.260 --> 00:10:29.940
While many Marvel Cinematic Universe fans&nbsp;
are beyond excited for Kang the Conqueror&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:29.940 --> 00:10:34.860
to make his debut in "Ant-Man &amp; the Wasp:&nbsp;
Quantumania," no one is more excited than&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:34.860 --> 00:10:40.020
Jonathan Majors himself. The character's role in&nbsp;
the film will have a very big impact on the MCU,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:40.020 --> 00:10:44.880
according to the film's director Peyton Reed in&nbsp;
an interview with Empire. Predictably, it's this&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:44.880 --> 00:10:49.500
impact on the MCU as a whole that initially drew&nbsp;
Jonathan Majors to the role in the first place.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:49.500 --> 00:10:54.480
Speaking to Marvel.com on his appearance in the&nbsp;
"Loki" finale, Majors said he was drawn to the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:54.480 --> 00:10:59.220
aspect of Kang's character that let him play&nbsp;
many different versions of the same villain.

00:10:59.220 --> 00:11:00.964
"Reincarnation, baby."

00:11:01.500 --> 00:11:05.760
On his appearance in "Quantumania,"&nbsp;
Majors had only one thing to say at&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:05.760 --> 00:11:09.042
Marvel's San Diego Comic-Con&nbsp;
panel in 2022, which was:

00:11:10.440 --> 00:11:14.520
Clearly, this is only the beginning&nbsp;
of Majors' journey as the character&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:14.520 --> 00:11:18.623
heading towards "Avengers:&nbsp;
The Kang Dynasty" in 2025.

00:11:18.623 --> 00:11:21.186
"See you soon."

